    "viz_teach": {
      "type": "splunk.markdown",
      "options": {
        "markdown": "## What this shows\nA synthetic NATO APP-6 / MIL-STD-2525D picture of 16 units, drawn as **milsymbol** markers. Three dashboard inputs change the symbol colour mode, size and frame without editing the SPL.\n\n## The SPL (abridged)\nThe first `mvappend` argument is shown once and the other 15 are elided. The full query, with all rows and HTML cards, is in the panel's data source (Open in Search).\n```spl\n| makeresults\n| eval data=mvappend(\n    \"50.5510|9.6800|sfgpuci----d|A/1-12 IN|TF IRON|INFANTRY|045|18|LEAD ASSAULT - AXIS NORTHEAST|30140800ZOCT24|50.5510N 9.6800E~~<tooltip HTML card>~~<popup HTML card>~~friendly_maneuver~~Friendly - Maneuver~~shield~~#1a4f8a\",\n    ... 15 more rows in the same format ...\n  )\n| mvexpand data\n| eval parts=split(data, \"~~\"),\n    core=mvindex(parts,0),\n    tooltip=mvindex(parts,1),\n    description=mvindex(parts,2),\n    layerGroup=mvindex(parts,3),\n    layerDescription=mvindex(parts,4),\n    layerIcon=mvindex(parts,5),\n    layerIconColor=mvindex(parts,6)\n| eval fields=split(core, \"|\")\n| eval\n    latitude=mvindex(fields,0),\n    longitude=mvindex(fields,1),\n    msSidc=mvindex(fields,2),\n    msUniqueDesignation=mvindex(fields,3),\n    msHigherFormation=mvindex(fields,4),\n    msType=mvindex(fields,5),\n    msDirection=mvindex(fields,6),\n    msSpeed=mvindex(fields,7),\n    msAdditionalInformation=mvindex(fields,8),\n    msDtg=mvindex(fields,9),\n    msLocation=mvindex(fields,10),\n    markerType=\"milsymbol\",\n    msSize=$msSize$,\n    msColorMode=\"$msColorMode$\",\n    msFrame=\"$msFrame$\"\n| fields latitude, longitude, markerType, msSidc, msSize, msColorMode, msFrame,\n         msUniqueDesignation, msHigherFormation, msType, msDirection, msSpeed,\n         msAdditionalInformation, msDtg, msLocation, tooltip, description,\n         layerGroup, layerDescription, layerIcon, layerIconColor\n```\n`$msSize$`, `$msColorMode$` and `$msFrame$` are dashboard tokens; if you see their current values here, Studio substituted them.\n\n## How it works\n1. `makeresults` + `mvappend` builds inline data. Each string is `core~~tooltip~~description~~layerGroup~~layerDescription~~layerIcon~~layerIconColor`.\n2. `mvexpand data` makes one row per unit. `split(data, \"~~\")` separates the parts; the `layer*`, `tooltip` and `description` fields are taken by position.\n3. `split(core, \"|\")` breaks the core into latitude, longitude, SIDC, designation and the other `ms*` fields.\n4. `markerType=\"milsymbol\"` plus the three token-driven fields (`msSize`, `msColorMode`, `msFrame`) are added to every row.\n5. `fields` keeps only what Maps+ reads and drops the helper fields (`data`, `parts`, `core`, `fields`).\n\n## Field formats and rules\n| Field | Expected format | Rule / gotcha |\n|---|---|---|\n| `latitude` | decimal degrees, numeric (e.g. `41.88`) | Exact lowercase name, required on marker rows. Only the first row is checked; if it has no `latitude`+`longitude` the panel shows an error. |\n| `longitude` | decimal degrees, numeric (e.g. `-87.72`) | Exact lowercase name. Longitude is negative west of Greenwich. Rows at 0,0 usually mean missing coordinates. |\n| `markerType` | `milsymbol` | Selects the military-symbol renderer. Other values are png, svg, icon, circle, custom. |\n| `msSidc` | symbol code string, e.g. `sfgpuci----d` | Chooses the symbol (`sf` friendly, `sh` hostile, `su` unknown in this data). |\n| `msSize` | number, here `25`, `35` or `50` | Symbol size from the Symbol Size input. |\n| `msColorMode` | `Light`, `Medium` or `Dark` | From the Symbol Color Mode input. |\n| `msFrame` | `\"true\"` or `\"false\"` | From the Show Frame input; keep as a string. |\n| `msUniqueDesignation, msHigherFormation, msType, msDirection, msSpeed, msAdditionalInformation, msDtg, msLocation` | text | Symbol labels and modifiers, set from the `core` fields. |\n| `tooltip / description` | HTML string | Hover card / click popup. Raw HTML: escape event text. |\n| `layerGroup / layerDescription` | name / HTML label | One layer-control entry per `layerGroup`. |\n| `layerIcon / layerIconColor` | Font Awesome name / CSS colour | Icon and colour beside the layer label. |\n\n## Try it\n- Pick **Dark** in Symbol Color Mode and **50** in Symbol Size.\n- Edit the `msSidc` of one row (e.g. `sfgpuci----d` to `shgpuci----d`) to turn a friendly infantry company hostile.\n\nStudio note: the panel options `msColorMode` is kept as the static `Light` from the original; the search tokens drive the per-row `msColorMode` field. Inputs auto-apply (no submit button), as in the original."
      }
    }
  },
